I've struck a problem: currently gem alchemy does not allow you to make
smoky or milky poitions (as they sometimes contain inhabitatnts). I'd
prefer to keep it that way, but then the question arises: what happens
if you dip the Stone into a smoky potion? If it turns into a different
gem, can that gem be used to make smoky potions?

One possibility would be to make the "spe" bit on a smoky potion
indicate whether it is capable of containing an inhabitant or not, but
then we have the question of merging potions. A randomly generated
smoky potion would no longer merge with a purpose-made smoky potion,
which would be a bit odd.

